    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0543" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v21/pg515"/>

                <head>327. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Consulate General in Salisbury<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d327-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-04-17T11:19:00-05:00">April 17, 1962,
                            11:19 a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>811. UNIP President Kenneth Kaunda discussed
                    Northern Rhodesian problems with Department officers April 13.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d327-f2"/> He appealed for U.S. <pb facs="0544" n="516"
                        xml:id="pg516"/> sympathy and political support, stressed that Welensky’s threat to use force to preserve
                    Federation should not be underestimated and declared that the present Federation
                    must be dissolved before useful discussions can be held concerning practical
                    relationships among the territories. Although outcome of Northern Rhodesian
                    elections in autumn uncertain, Kaunda confident that UNIP would emerge in better shape than any other party.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d327-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d327-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 745C.00/4-1762. Confidential. Drafted
                    by Dunham on April 16 and approved by Deming. Repeated to London and USUN.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d327-f2" n="1" xml:id="d327-f2-content">
                <p>A memorandum of conversation is ibid., 611.45C/4-2662.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
